WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.348
"By definition, only the Coward is capable of the highest heroism" - David Gemmell

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.189
For the coward fights, despite his weak nature.

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:16.079
Prince Allant, the son of King Allant, travels to the Boletarian Palace under the name "Ostrava", in order to hide his true identity.

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:21.599
The scourge has devastated the kingdom and as the player sets out to kill the arch demons,

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.080
Ostrava fights through the Boletarian Palace with the sole intention:

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:29.939
To find his father and to dispel the rumors that his father, the king

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.490
has become a demon.

00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:36.299
Ostrava is wise, but weak. He's lived a pampered life yet

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.739
he takes up the legendary weapons of a hero and attempts to fight his way to his father's throne.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:48.719
We first found Ostrava on a ledge, with no way back. He was surrounded by Dreglings, which were waiting to cut him down.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:56.579
"That was a bold jump, a surprise indeed. Well, now that you are here, pray thee, fend off these dreglings."

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.020
"My thanks for your brave rescue. I'm Ostrava of Boletaria."

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:18.360
We fought the Dreglings off as Ostrava watched. We can tell from the way he talks, he almost assumes...

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.360
it's our duty to rescue him.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:25.620
This will change, as Ostrava continues to discover her hopeless ease in the world around him.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.820
Much of his time is spent within the Nexus. Like many others, he has trouble finding the courage to leave.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.059
Ostrava, like you, is bound to the Nexus.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.699
Die in human form and you'll resurrect in an ethereal soul form.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:49.559
Demon souls allow you to keep your sanity while you're in this soul form, and a mature demon soul can restore your corporeal human form.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:55.079
But die in soul form and that's the end. You'll lose both your sanity and your life:

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:59.309
resurrecting as a black phantom. That's why death is such a fearsome thing.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.799
That's why Ostrava is afraid to leave the Nexus. But he came here for a reason. 
"At it's peak,

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.530
Boletaria was a grand kingdom.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.969
The King, his knights, and his subjects were modest and plain,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:17.250
but also steadfast and compassionate. In the distant Southern Kingdom,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.100
Boletaria was known as 'paradise on Earth'.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:28.920
But look at what has become of us now... I refuse to believe, that this is what father wished for our great land."

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.489
Ostrava progresses slowly, but surely.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.820
Always in fear of losing his life, but driven to reach his father's keep. With your help,

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.719
what would have been impossible becomes a possibility. "Over here!

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.390
It's me, Ostrava.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.859
Look at me, again surrounded by evil warriors.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.920
Could you, perhaps,

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.260
help me one last time?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.679
Clear out the soldiers at the far end of this passage,

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.000
if it pleases you.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.050
The Lord's Path, just down yonder, has degenerated into a feeding ground for flying dragons.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.840
Have your wits about you."

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.240
"Thank you. That makes twice.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.420
Thanks to you, I can now forge ahead."

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.060
In Boletaria, they speak of the two swords; "Demonbrandt" and "Soulbrandt".

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.139
One banishes that which befouls men, and the other banishes men himself.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:31.350
Dropped into the world along with the Old One, they seemed to symbolize the battle between man and his demons.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:37.109
Soulbrandt, the sword that grows in power the more demonic the soul that wields it, is missing.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:46.019
Ostrava is getting closer and closer to his father. Could it be that his father took up "that sword", the sword that banishes men?

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:52.440
"Help! Help! Soul-starved soldiers are after me!"

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.540
"Thank you for rescuing me."

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:10.379
"You saved my life... This is the third time, I am truly indebted to you."

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.700
"I must go.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.180
My father, the king, awaits me just over there."

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:26.700
The sad truth is that, once, King Allant was a benevolent ruler who cared greatly for his subjects.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.000
He fought diligently against the vile and the depraved.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.980
Alas, as he aged he became melancholy.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.489
Allant began a search for a method to expand his might.

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:44.209
His search brought him to the Nexus, where knowledge of the soul arts were bestowed upon him. This was not enough and eventually,

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.900
Allant awoke the Old One, which granted him unfathomable power.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.770
This power,

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.510
devastated his human form,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.049
transforming his body into a pathetic mutated creature.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.889
This is not Allant, this is a magnificent

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:04.728
demon that Allant fashioned, a doppelganger designed to lead the demon scourge and reap more souls to quench the thirst of the Old One.

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:07.728
The real king resides within the Old One.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.179
Believing that the Old One is a gift of mercy from God, in

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:16.250
his old age, Allant recognized that pain, evil and misery filled the world.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.479
It was so hopeless, that the only way to fight poison, was with poison.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:26.450
So Allant awoke the Old One, hoping for its deep fog to engulf the land and absorb every last soul.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.380
Only then, did he believe that human suffering would end.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.029
Despite all odds, Ostrava...

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:40.549
finally fights his way into his father's throne room. Past the soldiers who have had their souls stolen,

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:43.399
past the fat officials who torture and maim,

00:05:43.979 --> 00:05:48.409
past the dragons defending the king's keep, and up the final steps of his journey.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:54.380
Tragically, Prince Allant discovers that his father, has in fact, become a demon.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:06:01.310
This is not quite the truth, as the real Allant resides within the Old One, but, either way it is true that Allant;

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:06.979
once a benevolent ruler, is indeed responsible for the demon scourge that wiped out humanity.

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:09.660
" Oh, it's you, is it?

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.660
My father is up above...

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.300
Well, what's left of him anyway...

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:22.619
He's transformed into a fiendish demon... I began this quest in a search for truth,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.129
but it seems I was a fool to even try...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.230
Please,

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:35.550
kill my father. In his degenerated state, he can only bring peril to the lands.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.470
This key,

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.470
fits the Boletaria Mausoleum.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:46.920
Inside the mausoleum are my father's two swords; Soulbrandt and Demonbrandt.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.520
Use them to bring an end to this madness."

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:58.979
Overcome with despair, and before you can stop him, Ostrava kills himself in soul form.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.710
His black phantom appears shortly after.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.559
Ostrava found the truth, but it didn't bring him peace. His quest was for nothing,

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.650
yours wasn't.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:04.209
"On the first day man was granted a soul
And with it, clarity"
For in man, great potential was seen.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:12.639
Yet, "On the second day 
upon Earth was planted
an irrevocable poison
A soul-devouring demon."

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:18.250
For like the demon, man had an insatiable, destructive appetite for souls.
- from "Demon's Souls Story ► Prepare to Cry Trailer"

